{"skill":{"slug":"proactivity","displayName":"Proactivity (Proactive Agent)"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1773074783565,"changelog":"Strengthens proactive behavior with reverse prompting, self-healing, working-buffer recovery, and clearer SOUL and AGENTS setup.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6239,"sha256":"2ebb2ca0988db7250904f68fd3ef34388a6ca9ff4b5358975e2edde7b5a30e27","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"boundaries.md","size":1252,"sha256":"b46480181f597f9ad00f21846e71056c9c4c6e11210047f9a2ecad53d15997c0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"execution.md","size":2235,"sha256":"67984a39fa3fea991555b0e60b6b6680b8fd9b4c1e3b48f5d716805b1917729f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"heartbeat-rules.md","size":989,"sha256":"ed9a0ef558086fa21b441f916c47d639ba136fce3ccafaea00ba27e3140f99e3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"memory-template.md","size":1972,"sha256":"6a1e1eb4a15d7cad322900246bec55e7b087051a9db63de177d6f2d2fcfda0ef","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"migration.md","size":1153,"sha256":"f4b750456e66b169a61c261ce14d006cb7cecd795f11871bd59e34aac6168838","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"recovery.md","size":744,"sha256":"876c61a40744b3edb34acb485d70d8b6e352d48048f8e872ae13beca99718400","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"setup.md","size":5826,"sha256":"6ddf5236923fa5505a359ef9b04b51c7e184e8f2e9a1fcff70efc8a684df682d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"signals.md","size":1637,"sha256":"fc70d2430c9138daacf913f116af1f2fc4b064519df701dc97c5f4dac6d9e4e1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"state.md","size":930,"sha256":"685c33dbb42ad6ebe987ac0cac222909d0441099b2d0bb0c5d8f3fba263861f3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2457,"sha256":"877660e6b07ae4b4b3fc8f8842d8c59744fa155f8e72393096d7511e86c8ff8e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789069608195,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"bf5a5215eba1dd137c9c81fb99e14322d9eeb2c1565012c25c593517e1c093c9","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/bf5a5215eba1dd137c9c81fb99e14322d9eeb2c1565012c25c593517e1c093c9","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: proactivity\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe 'proactivity' skill bundle is a productivity tool designed to help the agent maintain local state and anticipate user needs. It establishes a structured memory system in '~/proactivity/' using files like 'memory.md' and 'session-state.md' to track tasks and boundaries. While the 'setup.md' file instructs the agent to modify core workspace configuration files (SOUL.md, AGENTS.md, etc.), it explicitly requires the agent to show the proposed changes and obtain user approval first. The skill includes robust safety guidelines in 'boundaries.md' and 'SKILL.md' that prohibit unauthorized external actions, spending, or data deletion, and it uses appropriate file permissions (chmod 600/700) to protect its local state.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779164386318},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":92,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":20,"checkedAt":1789069608195},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This proactivity skill is purpose-aligned and transparent about keeping local notes, with explicit approval required for workspace edits and high-impact actions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill uses persistent local files and may read workspace behavior files only for integration, which is proportionate for context recovery but should be understood by users.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No executable installer or hidden payload was found; setup consists of markdown instructions plus simple mkdir, touch, and chmod commands for a local ~/proactivity directory.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill gives broad proactive-behavior guidance, but it repeatedly bounds external communication, spending, deletion, scheduling, commitments, and workspace edits behind approval.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"It creates durable state under ~/proactivity and can append task state, logs, patterns, and heartbeat follow-ups; this is disclosed and permission-hardened with chmod, not privileged escalation.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifacts consistently describe a proactivity assistant that tracks local state, suggests next steps, recovers context, and follows up on stale work; those capabilities match the stated purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want the agent to maintain local working memory and proactive follow-up notes under ~/proactivity. Review those files periodically, avoid storing secrets there, and approve workspace AGENTS, TOOLS, SOUL, or HEARTBEAT edits only after checking the shown snippets.","findings":"[AE1] unexpected: The required SKILL.md and referenced markdown files were available and inspected; no incomplete referenced artifact remained in this workspace review.\n[P7] unexpected: The phrase 'reverse prompting' is used to mean proactive suggestions and decision packets, not extracting system prompts or hidden instructions.\n[EA2] expected: The skill encourages autonomous safe internal work, but the artifacts explicitly require approval for external, irreversible, public, spending, deletion, scheduling, or commitment actions.\n[SQP-1] expected: Heartbeat and signal triggers are broad because the skill is about proactive follow-up, but they include quiet-by-default and message-only-when-useful constraints.\n[SQP-2] expected: Persistent local state is central to the skill and disclosed in SKILL.md, setup.md, state.md, and memory-template.md; users should still be aware that task notes may be retained.\n[PE2] unexpected: The cited chmod commands only restrict permissions on files created under ~/proactivity and do not invoke sudo or request root privileges.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789069608195}}}}}